Description:
This is a terminal-based inventory management system for a workshop to track item storage and item borrowers. It uses a relational SQLite database to track tools, electronic components, and user borrowing activities. This program utilizes relational schemas using foreign keys across four distinct tables: users, categories, items, and borrow_logs.


How to use:
1. Clone the repository directly through Visual Studio Code.
2. Open the cloned folder in VS Code.
3. Open the Python script named "ty_jamesWilliam_labActivity5.py"
4. Run the code by clicking the run Python file and click on the Play button in the top right corner.
5. Use the terminal window to add your name (this is for the borrowing and adding option)
6. From the main loop, select what action you want to do by entering your selection in the terminal window
7. Enjoy using the program to navigate through several workshop items.

Features
1. User Sessions: Enter your name to start a session. New users are automatically registered.
2. View Inventory: Lists all items, shelf locations, the user who added them, quantity,  and a real-time list of current borrowers.
3. Add Items: Insert new items dynamically.
4. Borrow/Return: Track item checkouts.
5. Delete Items: Safely deletes items and their associated borrowing history to maintain database integrity.
